You can embed images in your HTML emails by including them in the [attachments](https://nodemailer.com/message/attachments) array and referencing them using the `cid:` (Content-ID) URL scheme.

2. Assign a unique [`cid`](https://nodemailer.com/message/attachments) (Content-ID) value to the attachment.

The **cid** value must be unique within the message.

Without an HTML body, `cid` attachments are delivered as regular attachments.

#### Basic example [​](https://nodemailer.com/message/embedded-images#basic-example)
The `cid` value in the attachment must match the value used in the HTML `src` attribute (without the `cid:` prefix).

```javascript
const message = {
  from: "Alice <alice@example.com>",
  to: "Bob <bob@example.com>",
  subject: "Inline image test",
  html: 'Embedded image: <img src="cid:logo@example.com" alt="Company logo"/>',
  attachments: [\
    {\
      filename: "logo.png",\
      path: "/path/to/logo.png",\
      cid: "logo@example.com", // matches the cid in the img src attribute\
    },\
  ],
};
```

#### Using a Buffer instead of a file [​](https://nodemailer.com/message/embedded-images#using-a-buffer-instead-of-a-file)
